From: Swift Linux <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] po/ab: put the space back after msgstr

One entry in the Abkhazian translation is written msgstr"..." with no
space before the string. GNU msgfmt reads it regardless, and that is
presumably why it was never noticed - but Buildroot's default host
gettext is gettext-tiny, whose parser insists on the space, and it
fails the file with no message at all:

    FAILED: [code=253] po/ab/LC_MESSAGES/gnome-session-47.mo

Every other .po in the tree is spelled msgstr "...", so this is a typo,
not a style. Add the space.

--- a/po/ab.po
+++ b/po/ab.po
@@ -222,7 +222,7 @@
 #. Translators: the 'fail whale' is the black dialog we show when something goes seriously wrong
 #: gnome-session/main.c:412
 msgid "Show the fail whale dialog for testing"
-msgstr"Иаашәырԥшы агха иазку ацҳамҭа змоу аиҿцәажәара, уи арҽеиразы "
+msgstr "Иаашәырԥшы агха иазку ацҳамҭа змоу аиҿцәажәара, уи арҽеиразы "
 
 #: gnome-session/main.c:413
 msgid "Disable hardware acceleration check"
